  "published": "2026-11-15T12:22:06.447Z",
  "releaseNotes": "Kazo OS 3.4.0-preview.3, changes for app developers:\n- Apps can carry their own libraries, and a shared library is loaded once. An app installed from a package can now have libraries of its own (another project, a NuGet package or a DLL): KazoOsPack puts them in the package and the OS loads them before the app, so such an app is no longer refused for a missing assembly. A library its author marks as shared (MSBuild property KazoOsSharedLibrary in the library's project) is loaded once for every app: the copy of an installed feature, otherwise the newest one of the same major version. When another copy is already loaded, the app keeps running with it and is shown as “Restart to finish”. An app whose shared library has another major version than an installed feature's copy is refused at installation, as is a library named like an assembly of the OS. For developers: nothing to declare in the app; kazoos-package.json lists the libraries.\n- Apps can use the services of an optional feature of the OS. A feature can now provide services to other apps: it declares ProvidedServices (an interface of a shared library and the class that implements it), and an app gets the instance with KazoFeatures.GetServiceAsync<T>(), or null when the feature is absent, disabled or outside the version range the app declares. The instance is created once per page, on the first request, in the feature’s own context and with its permissions. KazoFeatures.IsAvailable<T>(), GetStatusAsync<T>() and Changed tell why and when a service comes and goes. An app that declares the feature as an optional dependency stays in the catalog when the installed version is out of range. The build checks the declaration (KOSAPP0035) and that an app calling KazoFeatures declares a dependency (KOSAPP0034); a second feature that provides the same contract is refused at installation.\n- Optional features of the OS, installed for the whole machine. A package can now bring a feature (kind feature): one identity with its entry points (commands, windows, services), installed for every user by an administrator who approves its permissions once at installation; its entry points ask nothing at their first launch. The Store lists a feature its catalog marks kind: feature with the apps and offers “Install for everyone” only. Settings ▸ Applications lists each feature with its entry points. For developers: FeatureDefinition and FeatureEntryPoint in the SDK, one entrypoints/<suffix>.json per entry point in the package, diagnostics KOSAPP0032 and KOSAPP0033.\n- The Store offers the newest app version your Kazo OS runs, and a beta OS reads the beta catalog. The Store, kazopkg and the update check no longer offer an app version built for a newer Kazo OS than yours: they pick the newest version that runs here, so an app rebuilt for a newer SDK does not block an older OS. A prerelease of Kazo OS reads the beta channel of the official catalog (catalog-beta.json) and offers the beta versions of the apps; a stable Kazo OS reads catalog.json and never sees them.\n- App repositories call shared workflows and follow new Kazo OS versions by themselves. The kazoos-solution template now generates short workflows that call the reusable workflows of Kazo-ca/Os-AppTemplate (@v1), plus a \"Kazo OS SDK update\" workflow: when Kazo OS releases a version, the app moves to it, runs its CI, and is published (beta branch and beta channel for a pre-release; merged and published for a minor or major release; checked only for a patch). A red CI opens a TODO issue. A beta version (1.2.1-beta.1) goes to the beta channel of the catalog, and .github/scripts/bump-app-version.sh changes the app's version.\n- Kazo OS prereleases are published from the beta branch. Changing the preview number in build/Versions.props on the beta branch publishes a prerelease: Kazo.Os.* packages on nuget.org, a v<version> tag and a GitHub pre-release. main only accepts a stable version and beta only a prerelease version.\nRelease notes: https://github.com/Kazo-ca/Os/releases/tag/v3.4.0-preview.3",
